> Just wanna point out. One difficulty of Nethack is that
> there are only so many good artifacts. There are so many
> bad artifacts that finding an artifact is not necessarily a good
> thing, as it makes other artifacts harder to find.
> 
> We want at least half of the artifacts to suck, and the
> other half of the artifacts to be decent. :-p

This is oversimplifying the situation.

By definition, one artifact must be "best", and one artifact must be
"worst", and all others must fall inbetween.  That's a given, and
there's no way around it.

However, while the "best" artifact is clearly "useful", there is no
reason for the "worst" artifact to be so bad as to be "useless".  It is
possible to make it difficult to obtain the "best" artifact without
leaving the player holding Trollsbane as the alternative.

Thus, new artifacts should clearly come in somewhere above the "useless"
line, and some of the listed ones, as originally written, do not.

The problem is compounded when you add in the wish factor, thus making
all the "useless" artifacts seem like the proverbial rock in the gumball
machine.

There are already plenty of rocks in the gumball machine (often ending
in -bane); there is no need to create more.

